A useful negative control is h=y(y−x²)^3. It is monic in y of degree four, but has total degree seven. On M6_13/V1_1 its minimum D1 weight is −15/4; on V1_3 it is −11/2. In particular x²y³ is D1-allowed on both and excluded by total degree ≤4. This refutes an inference from monicity plus the given D1 floor. It does not assert a source-realized Jacobian pair. Also, when q=3 and K=4, [y^11]Q=3[y^3]h: the β2h and β3 blocks have y-degree ≤7 and ≤3. Hence an omitted y³ coefficient of h cannot simply be absorbed into those β blocks while keeping Q fixed. 

